#!/usr/bin/env -S python3 -B
"""Run one heavy command on a task machine, against the local tracked files.

Under env in .claude/settings.local.json, REMOTE_TASK_HOST names the task
machine's SSH destination and REMOTE_TASK_DIR the absolute path of the task
clone. REMOTE_TASK_TIMEOUT there caps the queue wait, in seconds. --wait reads
it from the environment. Set up the task clone once: clone the repository into
a dedicated directory, create .remote-task-workdir at its root, and install the
dependencies there.

--tool runs the program with the interpreter named on its #! line. Put the
interpreter on the task machine's login PATH. A line among the first ten of the
program, or of a sibling module that it imports, that reads
remote-tool-minimum-version: <X.Y> sets a minimum version. The highest applies.
"""

